hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"6271","Muhammad bin Salamah and Al-Harith bin Miskin told us, reading from him, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Humaid Ibn Abd al-Rahman and Muhammad Ibn al-Nu`man narrate on the authority of al-Nu`man ibn Bashir that his father brought him to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: I have given birth to my son as a boy who was mine? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Did your son eat his bee?” He said: No. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: So take it back. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6272","Muhammad bin Hashim told us, he said: Al-Walid bin Muslim told us, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Humaid bin Abd. Al-Rahman, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Numan, on the authority of Al-Numan bin Bashir, that his father, Bashir bin Saad, brought his son Al-Numan to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O Messenger of God, I have given birth to this son of mine, a boy who was mine. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Your sons have eaten Did you get married? He said: No. He said: Take it back. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6273","Amr bin Uthman bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Al-Walid, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, that Muhammad bin Al-Nu’man and Humaid bin Abd The Most Gracious, they told him, on the authority of Bashir bin Saad, that he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with Al-Numan bin Bashir, and said: I have given birth to my son. This is a boy, so if you see that I can execute him, will you execute him? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Did your children eat their honey?” He said: “No.” He said: “Then return it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6274","Muhammad bin Muammar Al-Basri told us, he said: Abu Amir, he is Abd al-Malik bin Amr, told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Bashir, that he had his son Nahla’s honey, and he wanted the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to bear witness, so he said: “ Did your son eat something like that? He said: No. He said: Give it back. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6275","Ahmad bin Harb told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, that his father They had a bee, and his mother said to him: “I bear witness to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, as to what you have given to my son.” So the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came and mentioned that. For him, the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, hated to bear witness to him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6276","Muhammad bin Hatim bin Nu’aym told us, he said: Hibban bin Musa al-Marwazi told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa On the authority of his father, that a good tidings came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: “O Prophet of God, I have given Nu’man a bee.” He said: “I have given His brothers? He said: No, he said: Return it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6277","Muhammad bin Abdul-Malik bin Abi Al-Shawareb told us, he said: Yazid told us, and he is Ibn Zurayi, he said: Dawud told us, and he is Ibn Abi Hind, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, who said: His father set off with him, carrying him to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: I bear witness that I have given al-Nu`man some of the money of so-and-so. He said: “You have given all your children the same as you gave al-Nu’man”? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6278","And Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, on the authority of Abdul Wahhab, he said: Dawud told us, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, that his father came The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, testified to him about a solution he made to him, and he said: “Did your son eat something similar to the one you made? He said: No. He said: So let me bear witness to this. Would you not be pleased if they were equal to you in righteousness? He said: Yes. He said: Then no. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6279","Musa bin Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Abu Usama told us, he said: Abu Hayyan told us, and his name is Yahya bin Saeed bin Hayyan. Al-Taymi, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, said: Al-Nu’man bin Bashir Al-Ansari told me that his mother, the daughter of Rawaha, asked his father for some talent from His money went to her son, so he kept it for a year, then it was his, so he gave it to him. She said: I will not be satisfied until she witnesses the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he greeted me for what you gave to my son. So my father took my hand, and I was a boy at that time. He came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God. By God, this man’s mother, the daughter of Rawaha, fought me a year ago over some of my money that was gifted to this son of mine, and it seemed to me, so I gave it to her. For him, and she liked that I should bear witness to what you have given him. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Bashir, do you have a son other than this?” He said: Yes, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Did you give to all of them something like what you gave to this son of yours? He said: No, the Messenger said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Then do not let me bear witness, for I do not bear witness to injustice.”"
"6280","Abu Dawud Suleiman bin Saif told us, he said: Ali told us, he is Ibn Ubaid, he said: Abu Hayyan told us, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, on the authority of Al-Numan bin Bashir said: My mother asked my father for some talent, so he gave it to me. She said: I will not be satisfied until I bear witness to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Then my father took my hand, and I was a boy that day, so he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, the mother of This is the daughter of Rawaha. She gave me some talent for him, and I gave it to him. She liked that we should witness that. He said: “ O Bashir, do you have a son other than this? He said: Yes. He said: So you gave him something like what you gave to this man? He said: No. He said: Then do not make me witness. For I do not bear witness to injustice.”"
"6281","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ubaid told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Amir, he said: I was told that Bashir bin Saad came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, my wife Amra bint Rawaha ordered me to give alms to She gave her son Numan in charity, and she ordered me to bear witness to that. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Do you have any children other than him?” He said: Yes, he said: Did you give them what you gave to this person? He said: No. He said: So do not make me witness to injustice. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6282","Ahmad bin Suleiman told us, he said: Abu Nu’aym told us, he said: Zakaria told us, on the authority of Amer, he said: Abdullah bin Utbah told me Ibn Masoud, H. Muhammad Ibn Hatim informed us, he said: Hibban informed us, he said: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Utbah bin Masoud, that a man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I gave alms to my son, so bear witness? He said: “Do you have another child? He said: Yes. He said: Did you give them as you gave him? He said: No. He said: I do not bear witness to injustice.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6283","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Fitr bin Khalifa, he said: Muslim bin Subayh told me, he said: I heard Al-Numan bin Bashir said: My father took me to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to testify to something he had given me. He said: “Do you have any other son?” He said: Yes, he described the entire thing with his hand and the palm of his hand, such-and-such, have you not leveled them all? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6284","Muhammad ibn Hatim informed us, he said: Hibban informed us, he said: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Fitr, on the authority of Muslim ibn Subayh, he said: I heard Al-Numan said while delivering the sermon: My father took me to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. To bear witness to the gift he had given me, so he said: “Do you have any children besides him?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “Make them equal.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6285","Yaqoub bin Sufyan told us, he said: Sulayman bin Harb told us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Hajib bin Al-Mufaddal bin Al-Muhallab, On the authority of his father, he said: I heard Al-Nu’man bin Bashir giving a sermon. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Be fair among your children. Be fair. \among your children\"""""""
"6286","Amr bin Yazid told us, he said: Ibn Abi Adi told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when a delegation from Hawazin came to him, and they said: O Muhammad, We are an origin and a family, and a calamity has befallen us that is not hidden from you, so be gracious to us. May God be gracious to you. He said: “Choose from your wealth. Or from your women and children. They said: You have given us a choice between our accounts and our wealth. Rather, we choose our women and our children. The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: As for what is mine and the sons of Abdul Muttalib, it is yours. And when I pray the noon prayer, stand up and say: We seek help. By the Messenger of God upon the believers, or Muslims, regarding our women and children. When they prayed the noon prayer, they stood up and said that, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May God bless him and grant him peace: Whatever is for me and the sons of Abdul Muttalib, is yours. The immigrants said: What is for us is for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And the Ansar said: Whatever is ours belongs to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Al-Aqra’ bin Habis said: As for me and the sons of Tamim, no, and Uyaynah bin Hisn said: As for me and Banu Fazara, no, and Al-Abbas bin Mirdas said: As for me and Banu Sulaym, no. Then Banu Sulaym stood up and said: You lied. Whatever we had belonged to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O people, return to them their wives and their children. Whoever holds on to any of this spoils has six obligatory duties from the first thing he must fulfill. God is upon us, and he rode his mount, and the people rode: Swear by us, so they took him to a tree, and she snatched his cloak, and he said: O one. People, return my cloak to me. By God, if you had a blessing like the Tihama tree, I would distribute it among you, and you would not find me stingy or a coward. And not a lie. Then he came to a camel and took a camel from its hump and a camel between his two fingers, then he said: Here, I do not have any of the spoils, not even this one. Except for the five, and the fifth will be returned to you. Then a man came up to him with a hair ball and said: O Messenger of God, I took this to make amends with it. A camel's calf is mine. He said: As for what was mine and that of the sons of Abd al-Muttalib, it is yours. He said: Have you reached this point? I have no interest in it. He rejected it and said: O people, give away the tailor and the thread, for the deceit will bring upon its people a disgrace, a curse, and a fire on the Day of Resurrection. \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"6287","Ahmad bin Hafs bin Abdullah Al-Naysaburi told us, he said: My father told me, he said: Ibrahim told me, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Arouba, On the authority of Amer Al-Ahwal, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No one shall return in A gift except a father from his child, and the one who returns in his gift is like the one who returns in his vomit.”"
"6288","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Hussein, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, he said: Tawoos told me, on the authority of Ibn Omar and Ibn Abbas attributed the hadith to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “It is not permissible for a man to give a gift.” Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Hussein, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of Tawoos, on the authority of Ibn Umar, and Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, I think he said: “It is not permissible.” Hussein did not doubt about the hadith except in: It is permissible, to give as a gift. Then he returns from it, except for the father in what he gives to his child, and the example of one who gives a gift and then returns from it, like a dog, eats until, when he is satisfied, he vomits. Then he returned to his vomit (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6289","Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Khalanji told us, he said: Abu Saeed told us, he said: Wahib told us, he said: Ibn Tawus told us, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The one who is repetitive in his vomiting is like a dog. He vomits and then returns to his vomit.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6290","Muhammad bin Hatim bin Nu’aym told us, he said: Hibban told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Nafi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Muslim, on the authority of Tawoos, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is not permissible for anyone to give a gift and then take it back, except from his own son.” \. Tawus said: I used to hear when I was young: he would return to his vomit"","" but I did not think that he was setting an example for him. He said: Whoever did that"","" then the like of him. Like a dog"","" it eats"","" then vomits"","" then returns to its vomit. (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"6291","Mahmoud bin Khalid told us, he said: Omar told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: Muhammad bin Ali bin Hussein told me, he said: Sa’id bin told me Al-Musayyib, he said: Abdullah bin Abbas told me, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The example of one who returns in his charity is like the example of one who returns in his charity. The dog returns in his vomit and eats it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6292","Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Abdul Samad told us, he said: Harb told us, he said: Yahya told me, he said: Abdul Rahman told me Bin Amr, that Muhammad, who is the son of Ali bin Hussein, the son of Fatima, daughter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, narrated to him, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The likeness of one who gives charity, then returns from it, is like a dog.” He vomited, then returned to his vomit and ate it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6293","Al-Haytham bin Marwan bin Al-Haytham bin Imran told us, he said: Muhammad told us, and he is the son of Bakkar bin Bilal, he said: Yahya told us, On the authority of Al-Awza’i, that Muhammad bin Ali bin Husayn narrated to him, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “The example of someone who goes back on his charity is like a dog that vomits, then goes back on its vomit.” Al-Awza’i said: I heard him narrating this hadith to Ata’ bin Abi Rabah. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6294","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, On the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “The one who returns to his gift is like a dog who returns to his vomit.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6295","Abu Al-Ash’ath told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Sa’id told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The one who returns in his gift is like the one who returns in his vomit.”"
"6296","Muhammad ibn al-Ala informed us, he said: Abu Khaled, who is Sulayman ibn Hayyan, narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “We have nothing like evil. The one who returns in his gift is like the one who returns in \His vomit\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"6297","Amr bin Zurarah told us, he said: Ismail bin Aliya told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “We have nothing like evil, one that returns to its blow, like a dog that returns to its vomit.”"
"6298","Muhammad bin Hatim bin Nu’aym told us, he said: Hibban told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “We have no equal to evil. The one who returns in his gift is like a dog in its vomit.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6299","Zakaria bin Yahya Al-Sijzi told me, he said: Ishaq told us, he said: Al-Makhzoumi told us, he said: Wahib told us, he said: Abdul told us Allah Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Anyone who is repetitive in his behavior is like a dog, vomiting.” Then he returns to his vomit.”"
"6300","Ahmad bin Harb told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Tawoos, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The one who returns in his gift is like the one who returns in his vomit.”"
"6301","Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam told us, he said: Ishaq al-Azraq told us, he said: Hussein al-Mu’allim told us about it, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of Tawoos, on the authority of Ibn Omar and Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is not permissible for anyone to give a gift. He will return therein, except for the father in what he gives to his child. The example of one who gives a gift and returns therein is like a dog, who eats until he is full and vomits, then Then he returned to his vomit.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6302","Abd al-Hamid bin Muhammad told us, he said: Mukhlid told us, and he is the son of Yazid al-Harrani, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of al-Hasan bin Muslim, on the authority of Tawoos, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is not permissible for anyone who gives a gift to take it back, except the father.” Tawus said: I used to hear the boys saying: O one who returns to his vomit, and I did not feel that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, struck that one. For example, until we heard that he used to say: “Like one who gives a gift and then takes it back,” and he mentioned a word that means: “Like a dog eating \His vomit\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"6303","Muhammad bin Hatim bin Nu’aym told us, he said: Hibban told us, Abdullah told us, on the authority of Hanzala, that he heard a peacock saying: Tell us Some of those who realized that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Like one who blows and then returns to his blow, like a dog that eats and then vomits.” Then he eats his own vomit.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6304","Hilal bin Al-Ala told us, he said: My father told us, he said: Ubayd Allah, who is Ibn Amr, told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, On the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Zayd ibn Thabit, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Slavery is permissible.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6305","Muhammad bin Ali bin Maymun Al-Raqqi told us, he said: Muhammad, who is the son of Yusuf Al-Faryabi, told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Zayd ibn Thabit, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “made the slave for the one who held it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6306","Zakaria bin Yahya told us, he said: Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Tawoos Perhaps it is on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “No enslavement, so whoever enslave anything is due to inheritance.”"
"6307","Muhammad bin Wahb Al-Harrani told me, he said: Muhammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Abu Abdul Rahim, who is Al-Jazari Khalid bin Abu Yazid, he said: Zaid, the son of Abi Anisa, narrated to me, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Do not monitor your wealth, for whoever watches something belongs to the one who watches it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6308","Ahmad bin Harb told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Tawoos, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The lifespan is for the one who frees it, and the slave is permissible for the one who frees it, and the one who returns his gift is like the one who returns it.” In his vomit"
"6309","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Tawoos, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said “The old woman and the slave woman are the same.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6310","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Ya’la bin Ubaid told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Tawoos, on the authority of Ibn Abbas said: “Neither slaves nor slaves are permissible. Whoever enslave something, it is his, and whoever enslave something, it is his.”"
"6311","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Tawoos, on the authority of Ibn Abbas said: “Neither slave labor nor enslavement is valid. Whoever maintains something or enslave it, his life belongs to the one who maintained it and supervised it.” And his death.” Hanzalah sent him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6312","Muhammad bin Hatim told us, he said: Hibban told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Hanzala, that he heard a peacock, saying: he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Slavery is not permissible, for whoever enslaves me is on the path of inheritance.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6313","Abdah bin Abd al-Rahim told me, on the authority of Waki’, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Zaid bin Thabit. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A lifetime is an inheritance.”"
"6314","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Hijr al-Madari, on the authority of Zaid He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The lifespan is for the heir.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6315","Muhammad bin Ubaid told us, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Hijr Al-Madari, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Umri is permissible.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6316","Muhammad ibn Ubaid informed us, on the authority of Ibn al-Mubarak, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Tawoos, on the authority of Zayd ibn Thabit, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The lifespan is for the heir.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6317","Muhammad ibn Hatim informed us, he said: Hibban informed us, he said: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Muammar, he said: I heard Amr ibn Dinar, narrating On the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Hijr al-Madari, on the authority of Zayd ibn Thabit, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The lifespan is for the heir.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6318","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, he said: I heard a peacock, He narrates, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “The lifespan is for the heir.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6319","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, he said: Amr bin Dinar told me, he said: I heard a peacock talking, about a stone. Al-Madri, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The lifespan is for the heir.”"
"6320","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Hijr al-Madri, on the authority of Zayd ibn Thabit, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “The lifespan is for the heir.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6321","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid informed us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Hijr al-Madari, on the authority of Zaid, that the Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He decreed that the lifespan should be given to the heir.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6322","Muhammad bin Ubayd Allah bin Yazid bin Ibrahim told us, saying: My father told me that a stronghold was offered to me, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, On the authority of Hijr al-Madri, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever maintains a thing, it is for its maintenance. His life and death, and do not expect anything, for whoever expects anything is on its way.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6323","Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Zayd bin Akhzam told us, he said: Muadh bin Hisham told us, he said: my father told me, on the authority of Qatada He said: Amr bin Dinar told us, on the authority of Tawoos, on the authority of Al-Hujuri, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Umrah is permissible.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6324","Harun bin Muhammad bin Bakkar bin Bilal told us, he said: My father told us, he said: Saeed told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Tawoos, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed life is permissible.” He ruled in Hudhayl (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6325","Muhammad bin Hatim told us, he said: Hibban told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, he said: Makhoul told us, on the authority of Peacock: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, afflicted the slaves and slaves.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6326","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Bastam bin Muslim told us, he said: Malik bin Dinar told us, on the authority of Ataa, on the authority of Jabir, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, addressed them and said: “Umrah is permissible.”"
"6327","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: I heard Qatada talking, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Umrah is permissible.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6328","Ahmad bin Sulaiman informed us, he said: Ubayd Allah informed us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Ata’, he said: The Messenger of God forbade May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “on the authority of Al-Amri and Al-Raqi.” I said: What is a slave? He said: A man says to a man: You have your life, so if you do it, it is permissible."
"6329","Muhammad ibn Hatim informed us, he said: Hibban informed us, he said: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik ibn Abi Suleiman, on the authority of Ata’, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever is given something for its life, it is his for his life and its death.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6330","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: “Do not oversee anything, and do not age it, for whoever enslave something, or age something, it belongs to his heirs.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6331","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Ata’, he said: Habib told me Ibn Abi Thabit, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “There is neither my life nor my enslavement, so whoever is appointed to do anything, or Watch him, for he is his, his life and his death.”"
"6332","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Muhammad bin Bakr told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told me, he said: Ata told me, on the authority of Habib Ibn Abi Thabit, on the authority of Ibn Umar, and he did not hear it from him. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Neither my life nor my slaves, so whoever is given life” Whatever it is, or whatever it is, it is his, his life and his death.” Ataa said: It is for the other (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6333","Abdah bin Abd al-Rahim informed me, he said: Waki` informed us, on the authority of Yazid bin Ziyad bin Abi al-Ja’d, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit. He said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade serfdom, and said: Whoever serfs my neck, it belongs to him."
"6334","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abu Asim told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, he said: Abu Al-Zubayr told me, that he heard Jabir, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever is given the life of something, it belongs to him, his life and his death.”"
"6335","Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Sadran Basri told me, on the authority of Bishr bin Al-Mufaddal, he said: Al-Hajjaj Al-Sawwaf told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, he said: Jabir told us, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Ansar, hold on to your property, meaning your property, do not occupy it. “For whoever takes care of something, its life and death belong to the one who takes care of it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6336","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: “Keep your possessions, and do not inhabit them. Whoever has his life inhabited, it is his, his life.” \His death\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"6337","Muhammad bin Al-Ala told us, he said: Abu Khalid told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The slave is for the one who holds it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6338","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Hushaym told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The old woman is permissible for her family, and the slave woman is permissible for her family.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6339","Mahmoud bin Khalid told me, he said: Omar told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, Ibn Shihab told me, and Amr bin Othman told me, he said: Baqiyya ibn al-Walid told us, on the authority of al-Awza’i, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever is given my life, it belongs to him and to his descendants. Whoever inherits it from his descendants shall inherit it.”"
"6340","Issa bin Musawar told us, he said: Al-Walid told us, he said: Abu Amr told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Jabir, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The life-long estate belongs to the one who inhabited it. It is for him and for his descendants. Whoever inherits it from his descendants shall inherit it.”"
"6341","Muhammad bin Hashim told us, he said: Al-Walid told us, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, and Abu Salamah, on the authority of Jabir. He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The lifespan belongs to the one who made it inhabited. It is for him and for his descendants. Whoever inherits from his descendants inherits it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6342","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahim told me, he said: Amr bin Abi Salama al-Dimashqi told us, on the authority of Abu Omar al-San’ani, on the authority of Hisham Ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Al-Zubayr, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Any man who gives life to another man will give me life.” “For him and for his descendants, it is his, and for whomever inherits from him from his descendants.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6343","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdul God, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever grants life to a man, an age will be given to him and to his descendants, his speech has cut off his rights. “And it is for him who was given life and for his descendants.”"
"6344","Muhammad bin Salamah and Al-Harith bin Miskin informed us of a reading from him, and I heard, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab On the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Jabir, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Any man who is given a long life, my life is for him and for his descendants, it is for the one who It will not be returned to the one who gave it, because he gave a gift that included inheritances.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6345","Imran bin Bakkar told us, he said: Abu Al-Yaman told us, he said: Shuaib told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Abu Salamah bin told me. Abd al-Rahman, that Jabir told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ruled: “Whoever performs a life of life for a man, my life will be given to him and his descendants. “It belongs to the one who inhabited it, having spent the night from its owner, who gave it what fell from God’s inheritance and right.”"
"6346","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Fudaik, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, On the authority of Abu Salamah ibn Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Jabir ibn Abdullah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He has decreed for him who has been given life my life for him.” And for his heel, it has a petal, of which the giver is not permitted to reach one part or the other.” Abu Salamah said: Because he gave a gift that included inheritances, so the inheritances were cut off under his condition. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6347","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Ya’qub told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Abu Salamah ibn Abd The Most Gracious, told him, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Any man who gives life to another man, my life will be given to him.” And for his successor, he said: I have given it to you and your successor, as long as none of you remain, for it belongs to whom I gave it to, and it will not return to its owner Because he gave a gift that included inheritances.”"
"6348","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid told us, he said: My father told us, he said: Saeed told us, he said: Yazid bin Abi Habib told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He decreed that the : For a man to give to another man, and to his offspring the gift, with an exception: If something happens to you and your offspring, then it belongs to me, and to my offspring, it is To whom it is given and to his successor.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6349","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled bin Al-Harith told us, he said: Hisham told us, he said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir told us He said: Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman told me, he said: I heard Jabir bin Abdullah, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “ “The lifespan belongs to the one to whom it was gifted.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6350","Yahya bin Durst told us, he said: Abu Ismail told us, he said: Yahya told us, that Abu Salamah told him, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The lifespan belongs to the one to whom it is gifted.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6351","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “I have neither my life nor a slave, so whoever is given life to do anything, it belongs to him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6352","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Issa told us, and Abdah bin Suleiman told us, they said: Muhammad bin Amr told us, he said: Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever is given care of something, it belongs to him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6353","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of al-Nadr ibn Anas, on the authority of Bashir ibn Forbidden, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “Umri is permissible.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6354","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muadh bin Hisham told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, he said: Sulayman bin Hisham asked me On the authority of Al-Umri, I said: Muhammad ibn Sirin narrated, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: “The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ruled that Al-Umri is permissible.” He said Qatada: And I said: Al-Nadr bin Anas narrated that Bashir bin Nahik, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Umri is permissible.” Qatada said: And I said: Al-Hasan used to say: Umri is permissible. Qatada said: Al-Zuhri said: When Al-Umari is appointed, then his descendants are appointed after him, so if he does not appoint his descendants after him, it belongs to the one who He makes his condition. Qatada said: Then Ata’ bin Abi Rabah was asked, and he said: Jabir bin Abdullah told me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “ “Umrah is permissible.” Qatada said: Al-Zuhri said: The caliphs did not decree this. Ataa said: So Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan decided on it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6355","Muhammad bin Muammar told us, he said: Hibban, who is Ibn Hilal, told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, and Ibrahim bin Yunus told me. Bin Muhammad, he said: My father told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Dawud, who is the son of Abi Hind, and the teacher’s lover, on the authority of Amr Bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is not permissible for a woman to give away her wealth if it is owned by She is protected from her husband.” The pronunciation is for Muhammad. Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Hussein al-Mu’allim told us, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, that his father told him , on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6356","Humayd bin Masada told us, he said: Yazid bin Zurayi told us, he said: Husayn al-Mu’allim told us, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of His father, on the authority of his grandfather, said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, conquered Mecca, he stood up to give a sermon, and he said in his sermon: “It is not permissible A woman is not given a gift, except with her husband’s permission.”"
"6357","Hanad bin Al-Sari told us, he said: Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Hani, on the authority of Abu Hudhayfah, on the authority of Abdul-Malik Bin Muhammad bin Bashir, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Alqamah Al-Thaqafi, he said: A Thaqif delegation came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and with them A gift, so he said: “A gift or charity? If it is a gift, then it is to seek the face of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and to fulfill The need, even if it is charity, is only for the pleasure of God. They said: No, but rather a gift. So he accepted it from them and sat with them. He questioned them and they questioned him, until he prayed the noon prayer with the afternoon prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6358","Abu Asim told us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I have decided not to accept a gift, except from a Qurayshi, Ansari, Thaqafi, or Dawsi.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6359","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Waki` told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, was brought meat, and he said: “What is this? It was said: Give it in charity to Bareerah, and he said: It is charity for her, and for us it is a gift.”"
"6360","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Ismail, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, that Abd al-Rahman bin Awf married a woman from The Ansar, so I met the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Mahim?” He said: I married a woman from the Ansar, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: “Have a sheep, even if it is a sheep.”"
"6361","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Affan bin Muslim told us, he said: Hammam told us, he said: Qatada told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Othman Al-Thaqafi, on the authority of a one-eyed man from Thaqeef who was called a favor, meaning he was praised well. If his name was not Zuhayr bin Othman, then I do not know what. Its name is that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The feast on the first day is a right, the second day is good, and the third day is reputation and hypocrisy.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6362","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “ A feast on the first day is a right, and on the second day it is honorable, and anything beyond that is hypocrisy.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6363","Muhammad bin Nasr al-Naysaburi told us, he said: Ayoub bin Sulaiman bin Bilal told us, he said: Abu Bakr bin Abi Uwais Madani told me, On the authority of Suleiman bin Bilal Madani, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed Al-Ansari Madani, on the authority of Humaid, that he heard Anas say: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace. He stayed with Safiyya bint Huyay for three days, until he married her. Then Safiyya was among those over whom the veil was imposed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6364","Ziyad bin Ayyub told us, he said: Ismail told us, he said: Abdul Aziz bin Suhaib told us, on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace \We invaded Khaybar"","" and we attacked it by force. Then the captives gathered"","" and Dihya came and said: O Prophet of God"","" give me a slave girl from the captivity. Then he said: 'Go"","" and take A slave girl"","" so he took Safiyya"","" the daughter of Huyay. Then a man came to the Prophet"","" may God bless him and grant him peace"","" and said: O Prophet of God"","" you gave Dihiyah to Safiyya. Bint Huyay"","" Sayyida Qurayza"","" and Al-Nadir! It is only suitable for you. He said: Call him for her"","" so he brought her. When the Prophet"","" may God bless him and grant him peace"","" looked at her"","" he said: Take a slave girl from the captivity. Other than her"","" he said: And the Prophet"","" may God bless him and grant him peace"","" freed her and married her"","" so Thabit said to him: O Abu Hamza"","" how truthful is she? He said: She herself. He freed her and married her. He said: Even when they were on the way"","" Umm Sulaim prepared it for him"","" so she gave it to him during the night. Then the Prophet"","" may God bless him and grant him peace"","" became a bride"","" and he said: Whoever has something"","" let him bring it"","" and he extended obedience"","" and made the man come. With aqat"","" and the man brought dates"","" and the man brought ghee"","" and they felt good"","" so it was the feast of the Messenger of God"","" may God bless him and grant him peace. Shuaib bin Al-Habhab followed him (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"6365","Imran bin Musa told us, he said: Abdul-Warith told us, he said: Shuaib bin Al-Habhab told us, he said: Anas told us, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: He freed Safiyya, married her, and made her dowry. He freed her, and made a burden on her. Al-Zuhri disagreed with them. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6366","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Abdullah Al-Naysaburi told me, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr Al-Humaidi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: Wael bin told us Dawud, on the authority of his son Bakr bin Wa’il, and Bakr used to sit with Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “told Ali Safiya with a stalk and dates.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6367","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, he said: “I have never seen the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, take pains to One of his wives. He did not blame Zainab for he had slaughtered a sheep.”"
"6368","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Waki’, he said: Issa bin Tahman told us, he said: I heard Anas say: “Did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace “peace be upon him and greet Zainab with bread and meat.”"
"6369","Ahmad bin Yahya bin Al-Wazir bin Sulayman informed us, saying: I heard Ibn Wahb saying: Sulayman bin Bilal narrated to me, on the authority of Humaid Al-Tawil, on the authority of Anas, said: “I ate a feast for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and there was no bread or meat in it.” It was said: Anything, O Abu? Hamza? He said: Dates and stalks."
"6370","Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn al-Wazir informed us, saying: Sa`id ibn Kathir informed us, that Suleiman ibn Bilal informed him, on the authority of Yahya ibn Saeed, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, said: “I witnessed the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a feast, in which there was neither bread nor meat.”"
"6371","Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Habib bin Al-Shahid told us, he said: Yahya bin Yaman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour bin Safiyya, on the authority of his mother, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave some of his wives a handful of barley.” Abdul Rahman disagreed with him, so he sent it on the authority of Sufyan. Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of his mother, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. . . Sent. He said: With two saa's (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6372","Ubayd Allah bin Sa’id told us, he said: Yahya al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Malik, he said: Nafi’ told me, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him and said: “If one of you is invited to a banquet, let him come to it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6373","Bishr bin Khaled Al-Askari told us in Basra, he said: I am Gandar, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Sulayman, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “If I were invited to a cubit, or to a cubit, and if an cubit or a cubit were given to me, I would accept.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6374","Suleiman bin Mansour Al-Balkhi told us, he said: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “When one of you is invited, he should respond. If he wants, he may eat it, and if he wants, he should leave it.”"
"6375","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “If one of you is called to a supplication, let him respond. If he is fasting, let him pray, and if he is not breaking his fast, let him eat.”"
"6376","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Al-Taffawi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “There is no good in food. The rich are invited to the wedding, and the poor are left out, and whoever does not respond has disobeyed God and His Messenger.”"
"6377","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Al-Araj, he heard Abu Hurairah say: “The worst food is the food of a feast; The rich will be invited to it, and the poor will be left behind, and whoever does not come to the invitation has disobeyed God and His Messenger.”"
"6378","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Bishr bin Al-Mufaddal told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Suleiman, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Abu Masoud, he said: A man from among us, called Abu Shuaib, prepared food and sent to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Come, you and five. He said: Will you permit me to eat? The sixth? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6379","Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Al-Hakam told me, he said: Othman bin Omar told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of my father Masoud said: A man prepared food for the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he sent to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “Bring me you and five.” He said: So he sent to him: “Give me permission on the sixth.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is a mistake, and the correct one before it is (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6380","Ubaid Allah bin Saad bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, he said: My uncle told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: He said: Anas bin Malik: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, became a bride with Zainab bint Jahsh, and he had married her in Medina, so he invited the people For food after the rise of the day, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sat, and some men sat with him after the people had risen, until the Messenger of God rose May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, so he walked, and I walked with him, until he reached the door of Aisha’s room, and he thought that they had left, so he returned, and I returned with him. So, when they were in their place, he returned, and I returned with him the second time, until he reached Aisha’s room. Then, when they had risen, he fought between me and him. cover, and lower the veil.”"
"6381","Qutayba bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha, that he heard Anas bin Malik, He says: Abu Talha said to Umm Sulaym: “I heard the voice of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, weak. I knew there was hunger in it. Do you have anything?” She said: Yes, so she brought out some barley tablets for him, then took her veil and wrapped the bread, then sent me to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him, and I found the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sitting in the mosque, and with him people, so I stood up to them, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: Did Abu Talha send you? I said: Yes. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to those with him: Get up, and I set off before them and came. Abu Talha, so I told him. Abu Talha said: O Umm Sulaim, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, has come, and we do not have any food. We will feed them. She said: God and His Messenger know best. So Abu Talha set off until he met the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he came. And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, until they entered, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Come, Umm Sulaim, what do you have? So she brought that The bread, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordered it, so it was crumbled, and Umm Sulaim squeezed her Akka, and she made it warm, then the Messenger of God said about it: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, whatever he wanted to say, then he said: Give permission to ten, so he gave them permission, and they ate until they were satisfied, then they left, then he said: He gave permission to ten, so he gave them permission, and they ate until they were satisfied, then they left. Then he said: Give permission to ten, so he gave them permission, so they ate until... They were satisfied, then they left, and the people were seventy or eighty men.”"
"6382","On the authority of Muhammad bin Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hamza Al-Sukkari, on the authority of Abdul-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Abu Salamah, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out at an hour when he would not go out and no one would meet him, so Abu Bakr came to him and said: “What brings you, Abu Bakr? He said: I went out to meet the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and to look at his face and to greet him, but I did not Soon, Omar came and said: What brought you, O Omar? He said: Hunger, O Messenger of God. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: And I have come. I found some of that, so they went to the house of Abu Al-Haytham bin Al-Tayhan Al-Ansari. He was a man who had many palm trees and winter trees. servants, but they did not find him, so they said to his wife: Where is your friend? She said: He went to find water for us. They did not wait until Abu al-Haytham came. With a waterskin he disturbed it, put it down, then came to join the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and ransom him for his father and mother, then he set off with them to His garden, so he spread out a rug for them, then he went to a palm tree, and brought a Qanoo, so he placed it, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Have you not purified yourself? For us, who made it fresh? He said: O Messenger of God, I wanted you to choose, or he said: Choose, from fresh and whole, so they ate and drank. Of that water, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “This, by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, is from the bliss about which you will be asked on the Day of Resurrection.” “Cool shade, good humidity, and cold water.” Then Abu al-Haytham went off to prepare food for them, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not slaughter a female animal.” Turn, he said: So he slaughtered a female goat or kid for them, and brought it to them, and they ate. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do you have a servant? He said: No. He said: If a captive comes to us, we will come to him, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought with two heads, without a third, so Abu al-Haytham came to him, and he said The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Choose from among them.” He said: O Prophet of God, choose for me. The Prophet said: “The one who is advised is trustworthy. Take this one. I will I saw him praying, and he entrusted him with kindness, so Abu Al-Haytham went to his wife and informed her of what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had said. She said: You cannot accomplish what the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said about him unless you free him. He said: He is freed, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said. He said: “Indeed, God has not sent a prophet or a caliph except that he has two entourage: an entourage that commands him to do what is right and forbids him from evil. “And a secret which you do not expect to be deceived, and whoever is protected from an evil secret, has been protected.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6383","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Ja’far bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Al-Ja’d Abu Uthman, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: The Messenger of God married May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. So he entered with his family. He said: So my mother, Umm Sulaym, made a harvest. He said: So I took it to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he greeted you, so I said: My mother greets you and says: This is a little for you from us. He said: Put it down. Then he said: Go, and invite so-and-so and so-and-so for me. So-and-so, and whomever I met, and he named some men. So I called whomever he named, and whoever I met. I said to Anas: How many were they? He said: And he mentioned a word, which means: about three hundred, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Let ten by ten shave themselves, and let everyone eat.” Then a group of people left, and a group entered. He said to me: O Anas, remove it. So I raised it, but I do not know when When I raised it, it was more, or when I lowered it?"
"6384","Musa bin Abdul Rahman Al-Antaki told us, saying: Mubashir bin Ismail Al-Halabi told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir. On the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Al-Harith Al-Taymi, he said: Atiya bin Qais told me, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told us He said the salaam after the Maghrib prayer, when he said: “O so-and-so, go with so-and-so, and oh so-and-so, go with so-and-so,” until I remained with five people, and I was the fifth of them. He said: Get up with me, so we entered upon Aisha, and that was before the veil was removed. He said: Feed us, O Aisha, so she brought an army for us. Then he said: Feed us, O Aisha, so she brought for us something like dung. Then he said: Give us something to drink, so she brought us a pot. Then he said: If you wish. You sleep with us, and if you wish, you can go to the mosque and sleep there.” We said: Rather, we will go to the mosque and sleep there. Shuaib bin Ishaq disagreed with him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6385","He said: Shuaib bin Shuaib bin Ishaq told me. He said: Abdul Wahhab told us. He said: Shuaib told us. He said: Al-Awza’i told us. He said: Yahya bin told us. My father Kathir, he said: Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman told me, he said: Qais bin Tukhfa al-Ghifari told me, he said: My father told me, that it was From the Companions of the Suffah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to come to us after the Maghrib prayer, and he would say: “O so-and-so, go with So-and-so, and you, oh so-and-so, go with so-and-so, until I remained with five people, of whom I was the fifth. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Go with me. So we set off with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, until we came to Aisha, and that was before the veil was drawn over her. He said: Oh Aisha, we lived, and she brought us a beast like cats. Then he said: O Aisha, we lived, and she brought us a beast like cats. Then he said: O Aisha. “Give us something to drink.” She brought us a ka’b, then he said: O Aisha, give us something to drink. She brought us a smaller ka’b, then he said: If you wish, you can spend water here. And if you wish, you can come to the mosque. We said: O Messenger of God, but we will come to the mosque.”"
"6386","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told us, he said: Al-Hasan bin Musa told us, he said: Shayban told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abd. The Most Gracious, that Ya’ish ibn Qays ibn Takhfah told him, on the authority of his father, he said: He was one of the people of the description. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “O so-and-so, take this with you. O so-and-so, take this with you. There were four days left, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to us: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Go, so we set off until we came to Aisha’s house, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Aisha: Give us food, so she came. With a gushishah, so we ate, then he said: O Aisha, feed us. Then she brought a camel like peat, then he said: O Aisha, give us something to drink. She came with a mug, so we drank, then he said: O Aisha, give us something to drink. She brought a small cup containing milk, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to us: He, peace and blessings be upon him: “If you wish, you can spend the night here, and if you wish, then go to the mosque.” We said: “Rather, we will go to the mosque.”"
"6387","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, on the authority of Muadh bin Hisham, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, he said: Abu Salamah told me Ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Ya’ish ibn Takhfa ibn Qais al-Ghifari, who said: My father was one of the people of the Suffah, so he made the man go with the other. And with the two men, until I remained the fifth of five with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Go with us to Aisha's house, so we set off, and he said: O Aisha, feed us. She brought a group of people, and we ate. Then he said: O Aisha, feed us. She came with a small cup like a cat, so we ate, then he said: O Aisha, give us something to drink. She brought a small cup, so we drank, then he said: If you wish, you may perform prayers in prayer, and if you wish, you may go to the mosque.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6388","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Ya’qub bin Abdul Rahman Al-Iskandarani told us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, he said: I heard Sahl, saying: He came Abu Usayd al-Saadi, he invited the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to his wedding, and his wife was their servant at that time, and she was the bride. He said: “Do you know what I gave the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to drink? I soaked dates for him during the night in a jug.”"
"6389","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Ismail told us, he said: Humayd told us, on the authority of Anas, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stayed between Khaybar And the city was being built for three days by Safiyya bint Huyay, so I invited the Muslims to his feast, but there was neither bread nor meat in it. He ordered With fresh fruits, dates, acorns, and ghee were thrown at her, and that was his feast.”"
"6390","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Muadh bin Hisham told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Yunus, who is the cobbler, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, He said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, did not eat in a bowl, nor in a sausage, nor in his bread. I said: What did they eat? He said: On.” This travel.” Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Muadh bin Hisham, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Yunus. . . Likewise, he said: I said to Qatada: What did they eat? He said: On travel"
"6391","Musa bin Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Husayn told us, on the authority of Zaida, he said: Waqid told us, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was given as gifts: a speck, a fat animal, and a lizard. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “As for these, they will not be In our land, whoever among you likes to eat, let him eat on his own.” And he did not eat from it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6392","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Al-Muthanna told us, he said: I am Talha bin Nafi’, on the authority of Jabir, he said: He took The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took me to his house with my hand. When we finished, they brought out a plate with a piece of bread on it, and he ate. He said: “As for the one who Adam? They said: No, except some vinegar. He said: Vinegar is the best of Adam. Jaber said: I still love him since I heard it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6393","Amr bin Uthman told me, he said: Baqiya told us, on the authority of Buhair, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, he said: The Ansar cast lots for their homes, as to which of them would shelter the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so Abu Ayyub cast lots for them, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took refuge in him. May God bless him and grant him peace. Whenever food was given to him, it would be given as a gift. Then Abu Ayyub went to his family and found a piece of food containing greens and onions. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent it with it. Abu Ayyub went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: What prevented you from doing so? The piece that was given to us? He said: “I saw onions in it. Abu Ayyub said: Are onions not permissible?” He said: Yes, so eat them. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He will cover me with something that does not cover you.” Jabir ibn Samurah disagreed with him."
"6394","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khalid told us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Jabir bin Samra, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, he said: A piece of bread containing garlic was sent to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he did not eat it. He sent it to me, and I said: O Messenger of God, You did not eat some of it, and you sent it to me. Is it forbidden? He said: “No, but I hated its smell.” He said: “I hate what you hate.”"
"6395","Yahya bin Mukhlid Al-Baghdadi told us, saying: Al-Mu’afāf, who is Ibn Imran Al-Mawsili, told me on the authority of Saif, who is Ibn Sulayman. Al-Makki, he said: I heard Mujahid, speaking on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Laila, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He says: “Do not wear silk or brocade, and do not drink from vessels of gold and silver, and do not eat from vessels made from them, for they will be yours in the Hereafter. And for them in this world.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6396","Ahmad bin Hafs bin Abdullah Al-Naysaburi told us, he said: My father told me, he said: Ibrahim, he is the son of Tahman, told me, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Anas ibn Sirin, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade eating. And drinking from vessels of gold and silver.”"
"6397","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: I am Ali, meaning Ibn Mushar, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: Abu Humaid came Al-Saadi went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with milk in a cup, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Did you not leaven it? \It will come back to him\"""""""
"6398","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Muadh bin Hisham, he said: my father told me, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, he said: “What The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ate on a plate, and he said again: “Not on a table, nor in a crib, nor does he have any unleavened bread.”"
"6399","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala informed us, on the authority of Khalid, he said: Shu`bah, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, on the authority of Anas, he said: “I did not see The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was intimate with any of his wives. He had never been intimate with Safiyya.” Thabit said: What was fed? He said: Bread and meat, until they left it. He said: How true is it? He said: He freed her and married her. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6400","Abu Bakr bin Nafi’ told us, he said: Bahz told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Thabit told us, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him Then a piece of barley bread was brought to it, with a toothpaste on it. They began to eat, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, the good is the best of the Hereafter.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6401","Muhammad bin Qudamah told us, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “The family was not satisfied Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, from the time he came to Medina for food for three successive nights, until he was arrested.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6402","Al-Fadl bin Sahl Al-Araj told us, he said: Abdullah bin Amr Abu Muammar told us, he said: Abdul-Warith told us, he said: Saeed bin Abi Arouba told us. On the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He did not eat with traitors until he died, nor did he eat bread.” He was afflicted until he died.”"
"6403","Harun bin Ishaq told us, he said: Abdah told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Najiya al-Khuza’i, he said: I said: “O Messenger of God, how? What should I do with the spoiled body? He said: “Slaughter it, then dip its soles in its blood, then leave it between the people and let them eat it.”"
"6404","Kathir bin Ubaid told me, he said: Baqiya told us, on the authority of Thawr bin Yazid, on the authority of Salih bin Yahya bin Al-Miqdam bin Maadi Karib, On the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Khaled ibn al-Walid, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “forbade eating the meat of horses and mules, And donkeys, and every fanged wild animal.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6405","Qutayba bin Saeed and Ahmad bin Abdah told us, and the wording is his, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ali, on the authority of Jabir “On the Day of Khaybar, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade eating the meat of donkeys, and gave permission for horses.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: I do not know that anyone agreed with Hammad bin Zaid with Muhammad bin Ali. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6406","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, fed us meat horses, and forbade us from the meat of donkeys.”"
"6407","Al-Hussein bin Harith told us, he said: Al-Fadl bin Musa told us, on the authority of Hussein, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, and on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, fed us horse meat on the Day of Khaybar. And he forbade us from donkey meat.”"
"6408","Qutaibah told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of Fatima bint al-Mundhir, on the authority of Asma’, she said: “We sacrificed A horse at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we ate its meat.”"
"6409","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Muhammad bin Bishr, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace “He forbade the meat of domestic donkeys on the Day of Khaybar.” Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Muhammad bin Ubaid, he said: Ubaid Allah told us, on the authority of Nafi’, and Salim, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. . . The same, and he did not say: Khaybar (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6410","Amr bin Uthman bin Saeed told me, he said: Baqiya told us, on the authority of Buhair, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr, on the authority of Abu Tha’labah He told them that they had marched with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to Khaybar, and the people were hungry, and they found there a number of donkeys. Humans, so the people slaughtered some of it, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, narrated that, so he ordered Abd al-Rahman bin Awf, and he announced to the people: “Don’t The meat of human donkeys is not permissible for one who bears witness that I am the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"6411","Amr bin Yazid told us, he said: Bahz told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, he said: Abdullah bin Dinar told me that he heard Ibn Omar, he said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a lizard, and he said: What do you say about this? He said: “I do not eat it, nor do I prohibit it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6412","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Zayd bin Wahb, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Azib, On the authority of Thabit bin Wadi’ah, that a man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a lizard and said: “A nation has been transformed, God knows best.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6413","Amr bin Yazid told us, he said: Bahz told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, he said: Adi bin Thabit told me, he said: I heard Zayd bin Wahb. He narrates, on the authority of Thabit bin Wadi’ah, who said: A man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a piece of fog, and he began to look at it and turn it over. He said: “A nation has been transformed. It is not known what it did, and I do not know. Perhaps this is one of them.”"
"6414","Suleiman bin Mansour informed us, saying: Abu Al-Ahwas Salam bin Sulaym narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Zayd bin Wahb, on the authority of Thabit bin Yazid He said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey, and we stayed at a place, and the people were covered in mist, so I took mist from her. So I roasted it, then I brought it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he took a stick and counted his fingers with it, then said: “A nation from among the Children of Israel You have transformed animals on the ground, and I do not know which animals they are. I said: O Messenger of God, the people have eaten from them. He said: So he was not commanded to eat them. And he did not forbid.” Abu Dawud Sulaiman bin Saif told us, he said: Muhammad bin Sulaiman al-Harrani told us, he said: Abu Ja`far al-Razi told us, on the authority of Husayn bin Abd. Al-Rahman, on the authority of Zayd bin Wahb, on the authority of Thabit bin Yazid bin Wadi’ah Al-Ansari, who said: We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a campaign. Khaybar, and we were hit by fog. . . The chain of the hadith (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6415","Harun bin Abdullah told us, he said: Ma’n told us, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Umamah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, That Khalid bin Al-Walid entered the house of Maimuna, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and brought a preserved lizard, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, fell in love with it. Then some of the women who were in Maimunah’s house said: Tell the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, what he wants to eat from. They said: It is him. A lizard raised his hand, and I said: Is it forbidden, O Messenger of God? He said: “No, and it was not in the land of my people, so I found that it was spared, so I guarded it and ate it while the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was watching.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6416","Harun bin Abdullah told me, on the authority of Abu Dawud, he said: Zuhair narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Saad bin Iyadh, on the authority of Abdullah, He said: “The most beloved Iraq to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was Iraq the sheep.”"
"6417","Yusuf bin Issa told us, he said: I am Al-Fadl bin Musa, he said: I am Mas’ar, on the authority of Abu Sakhrah, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah said: “I spent the night with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace,” and he was passing me by, until Bilal gave the call to prayer, so he asked The knife, and he said: “What does he have? His hands became wet.”"
"6418","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Abu Aoun told me, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Shaddad, he said: Marwan said: How do we ask, when among us are the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? So he sent for Umm Salamah, and she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, left, so I pulled out a handful of pot for him, and he ate from it, then went out.” \to prayer\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"6419","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Mis’ar told us, on the authority of a man of understanding, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ja’far, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “The best meat is the back meat.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6420","Saeed bin Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Thana is beloved, and he is the son of Musa Abu Salih al-Farra, he said: I am Ibn al-Mubarak, on the authority of Osama Ibn Zayd, on the authority of Al-Fadl Ibn Al-Fadl, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, on the authority of Daba’ah bint al-Zubayr, that she slaughtered a sheep in her house, Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent to her asking us to feed him from your sheep, and she said: “We only have the neck, and I am ashamed to eat it.” He was sent to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with Al-Raqabah. The Messenger returned and informed the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Go back. To it, then say: “Send with it, for it is the guide to the sheep, the closest sheep to goodness, and the furthest from harm.”"
"6421","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, on the authority of Safwan bin Issa, he said: Ibn Ajlan told us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: I slaughtered for the Messenger of God God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a sheep. He said: “He gave me the arm, and I gave him the arm. He said: He gave me the arm, and I gave him the arm. Then he said: Give me the arm. I said: O Messenger of God, the sheep has only two arms. He said: If I sought it, I would find it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6422","Wasil bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, and his name is Yahya bin Saeed bin Hayyan, on the authority of Abu Zar’ah Ibn Amr, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came one day, and the arm was raised to him, and he was amazed. So he swallowed some of it.”"
"6423","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told me, on the authority of Shuaib, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Hilal, on the authority of Ibn Abi Rafi’, on the authority of Abu Ghatafan, narrated to him on the authority of Abu Rafi’, who said: “I was grilling the belly of a sheep for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He has performed ablution for prayer, so he eats from it, then goes out to pray, but does not perform ablution.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6424","Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha, that he heard Anas bin Malik say: A tailor invited the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, for food he had made. Anas said: So I went with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to that food. Then he brought to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, bread made from barley and broth containing some medicine and some oil. Anas said: “Then I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, followed the scavengers around the newspaper, and I have not stopped loving scavengers since that day.”"
"6425","Salih bin Adi told me, he said: Al-Sumayd bin Wahib narrated to us, he said: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Zayd, on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, peace be upon him, prayed May God bless him and grant him peace: “He was admired by the scavengers.” Muhammad ibn Ja’far disagreed with him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6426","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja`far told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, he said: I heard Anas say: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, loves animals.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6427","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Hafs told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Hakim bin Jabir, on the authority of his father, he said: I entered On the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I saw “with him an animal being cut down. I said: What is this? He said: We multiply our food with it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6428","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Jarir, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Utaiba, on the authority of Al-Hasan Al-Urni, on the authority of Amr bin Harith On the authority of Saeed bin Zaid, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Truffles are part of the manna that God sent down to Moses, and its water is a cure for the eyes.” \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"6429","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Al-Nadr bin Shumail told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: I am Abd al-Malik bin Umair, he said: I heard Amr Bin Harith, said: I heard Saeed bin Zaid bin Amr bin Nufayl, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Truffles are from Manna, and its water is a cure for the eyes.”"
"6430","Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi told us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Shabib, he said: I heard it from Shahr bin Hawshab, so I asked him, and he said: I heard it from Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, so I met Abd al-Malik, and he told me on the authority of Amr ibn Harith, on the authority of Saeed bin Zaid said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Truffles are a type of manna, and their water is a cure for the eyes.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6431","Abu Bakr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdullah bin Aoun told us, he said: Abu Ubaidah told us, he said: Abdul Jalil bin Atiya told us, on the authority of A month ago, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Truffles are part of manna, and their water is a cure for the eyes.”"
"6432","Ali bin Al-Hussein told us, he said: Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Shahr bin Hawshab, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Sheep, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out to them, and they were mentioning truffles, and some of them said: smallpox. Earth, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Truffles are from manna, and its water is a cure for the eyes, and the ajwa is from Paradise, and it is a cure.” \of poison\"""""""
"6433","Nusayr bin Al-Faraj told us, he said: Muadh bin Hisham told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Shahr bin Hawshab, on the authority of my father Hurairah, that the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Truffles are from manna, and its water is a cure for the eyes, and ajwa is from Paradise, and it is A cure from poison,” and on the authority of Muhammad ibn Bashar, on the authority of Muadh ibn Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Bashar, on the authority of Abu Abd Al-Samad Abd al-Aziz bin Abd al-Samad, on the authority of Matar al-Warraq, both of them are Qatada and Matar, on the authority of Shahr bin Hawshab, with it (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6434","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul-Ala bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Shahr bin Hawshab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Truffles are leftover from the manna, and their water is a cure for the eyes.” The disagreement over Abu Bishr (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6435","Muhammad ibn Bashhar told us, in his hadith, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Jaafar, he said: Shu`bah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Shahr, on the authority of Abu Huraira, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Truffles are part of manna, and their water is a cure for the eyes.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
